            <ArticleTitle>Gastric bezoar after laparoscopic Roux-en-Y gastric bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>365-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Gastric bezoar is an uncommon complication following Roux-en-Y gastric bypass (RYGBP). We report two cases of bezoar formation that occurred following laparoscopic RYGBPs. In both cases, the patients presented with abdominal pain, nausea, and &quot;frothy&quot; vomiting. The patients were successfully treated by endoscopic fragmentation and removal of the bezoar.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
